---
<<declare $The_Seagull_CurrentLv = 1>>

===

title: Bruno_Upgrade
position: 100,-312
---

Bruno : Hi! How can I Help you?
-> I want to upgrade building.
    <<jump Select_Building_to_Upgrade>>
-> Nothing.
===

title: Select_Building_to_Upgrade
position: -32,-65
---
Bruno : Sure! Which one?
-> The Seagull Inn.
    <<jump Upgrade_The_Seagull_Inn>>
-> On second thought, I'd rather not do it.
    <<jump Cancel_Upgrade>>
===

title: Upgrade_The_Seagull_Inn
position: -354,-66
---
<<if $The_Seagull_CurrentLv > 0 && $The_Seagull_CurrentLv < 3>>
    <<if $The_Seagull_CurrentLv == 1>>
        Bruno : 2,000 coins.
        -> Here you are.
            <<requestUpgradeBuilding "The Seagull Inn_lv.1">>
            <<set $The_Seagull_CurrentLv += 1>>
            <<jump Admited_Upgrade>>
        -> I'll cancel it.
            <<jump Cancel_Upgrade>>
    <<endif>>
    <<if $The_Seagull_CurrentLv == 2>>
        Bruno : 3,000 coins.
        -> Here you are.
            <<requestUpgradeBuilding "The Seagull Inn_lv.2(Clone)">>
            <<set $The_Seagull_CurrentLv += 1>>
            <<jump Admited_Upgrade>>
        -> I'll cancel it.
            <<jump Cancel_Upgrade>>
        
    <<endif>>
<<else>> 
    <<set $The_Seagull_CurrentLv = -1>>
    Bruno : Now you can't upgrade this building anymore.
    -> Back to select building.
        <<jump Select_Building_to_Upgrade>>
    -> Ok then.
<<endif>>
===

title: Admited_Upgrade
